            <ArticleTitle>Early clinical results of the use of radiofrequency lesioning in the treatment of plantar fasciitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>215-9; discussion 256</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In this paper the authors discuss plantar fascial heel pain, including its etiology and treatment. The results of a retrospective study using radiofrequency lesioning on plantar fascial heel pain are presented and discussed. Thirty-nine patients were treated with radiofrequency lesioning, and 92% of the patients experienced complete resolution of symptoms following the procedure.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
